rgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/permelin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/permelin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/permelin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"It's been a couple of years since I looked at this, but IIRC, yes.\n\nThe issue is that `lm_pos` is the center of the object, so the object's AABB can intersect with the lightmap but still be ignored if the center is outside it.\n\nThis is what I wrote about this two years ago:\n> I think you could just remove this check. IIRC, this code path will not be hit unless the lightmap has been assigned to the object, and that will only happen if the lightmap and object already intersect. Quitting early is redundant.","created_at":"2026-05-13T16:11:25Z","updated_at":"2026-05-13T16:11:26Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117773#discussion_r3235768993","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117773","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3235768993"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117773#discussion_r3235768993"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117773"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3235768993/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":2087,"original_start_line":2087,"start_side":"LEFT","line":2089,"original_line":2089,"side":"LEFT","in_reply_to_id":3235276974,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":17,"position":17,"subject_type":"line"}]